+// DisplayXR browser#117: true iff HTMLCanvasPainter will register this
+// element's kInline3dWeave rect on the canvas's OWN cc layer during this same
+// paint — the ForeignLayer path.
+//
+// Patch 0060 stopped ReplacedPainter FORCING a background display item into
+// existence for an inline-3d-only canvas, and that killed the duplicate for a
+// BARE canvas. It did not kill it for the canvas the inline-3D SDK actually
+// creates: the viewer attaches a non-passive `wheel` listener plus pointer
+// handlers to every tile, so InsideBlockingWheelEventHandler() /
+// HasEffectiveAllowedTouchAction() make the background item exist anyway
+// (ShouldPaintBoxDecorationBackground's earlier conditions, above). The chunk
+// it produces then carries a SECOND copy of the same TrackedElementId, merged
+// into the enclosing PictureLayer — a different LayerImpl with a different
+// stable_id_for_shared_quad_state(). Viz saw the element twice with two layer
+// ids every frame, had to arbitrate, and when it kept the PictureLayer copy
+// (which draws no canvas quad) the identity join could not succeed at all: the
+// whole weave silently ran on the geometric overlap fallback, whose ratio is
+// the element's visible fraction, so a tile below ~70% visibility matched
+// nothing and the page drew its raw SBS buffer.
+//
+// So: when the pixels ride their own layer, that layer owns the rect and the
+// chunk must not carry a copy. When they do NOT — an unaccelerated canvas,
+// printing, or a paint that omits compositing info — HTMLCanvasPainter takes
+// the DrawingRecorder path, registers nothing, and the chunk-borne copy is the
+// only one there is; it must survive untouched.
+bool Inline3dWeaveRectRidesOwnLayer(const LayoutReplaced& layout_replaced,
+                                    const PaintInfo& paint_info) {
+  const auto* canvas = DynamicTo<HTMLCanvasElement>(layout_replaced.GetNode());
+  if (!canvas || !canvas->GetTrackedElementSubRect(
+                     viz::TrackedElementFeature::kInline3dWeave)) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  // Mirrors HTMLCanvasPainter::PaintReplaced's foreign-layer conditions.
+  return canvas->ContentsCcLayer() && !paint_info.ShouldOmitCompositingInfo() &&
+         !canvas->IsPrinting();
+}
